Core KPI Measures
1. Total Revenue
Total Revenue =
SUM(orders[price_usd])

Result: ~$1.94M
2. Total Profit

For product-level profitability, use order_items:

Total Profit =
SUM(order_items[price_usd]) - SUM(order_items[cogs_usd])

Result: ~$1.22M

3. Total Orders
Total Orders =
DISTINCTCOUNT(orders[order_id])

Result: ~32K

4. Total Sessions
Total Sessions =
DISTINCTCOUNT(website_sessions[website_session_id])

Result: ~473K

5. Conversion Rate
Conversion Rate =
DIVIDE(
    [Total Orders],
    [Total Sessions],
    0
)

Then format it as Percentage.

Result: ~6.83%

6. Revenue per Session
Revenue per Session =
DIVIDE(
    [Total Revenue],
    [Total Sessions],
    0
)

Result: ~$4.10

Product Analysis Measures
7. Total COGS
Total COGS =
SUM(order_items[cogs_usd])
8. Profit Margin
Profit Margin =
DIVIDE(
    [Total Profit],
    [Total Revenue],
    0
)

Format as Percentage.

9. Total Refunds
Total Refunds =
SUM(order_item_refunds[refund_amount_usd])
10. Refund Rate
Refund Rate =
DIVIDE(
    [Total Refunds],
    [Total Revenue],
    0
)

Format as Percentage.

Useful E-commerce Measures
11. Average Order Value
Average Order Value =
DIVIDE(
    [Total Revenue],
    [Total Orders],
    0
)
12. Orders per Session
Orders per Session =
DIVIDE(
    [Total Orders],
    [Total Sessions],
    0
)
13. Total Pageviews
Total Pageviews =
DISTINCTCOUNT(website_pageviews[website_pageview_id])
14. Pages per Session
Pages per Session =
DIVIDE(
    [Total Pageviews],
    [Total Sessions],
    0
)
New vs Repeat Sessions

If is_repeat_session exists in website_sessions:

15. New Sessions
New Sessions =
CALCULATE(
    [Total Sessions],
    website_sessions[is_repeat_session] = 0
)
16. Repeat Sessions
Repeat Sessions =
CALCULATE(
    [Total Sessions],
    website_sessions[is_repeat_session] = 1
)
17. Repeat Session Rate
Repeat Session Rate =
DIVIDE(
    [Repeat Sessions],
    [Total Sessions],
    0
)
Your final Measures folder

I recommend keeping these 12 main measures in your report:

Total Revenue
Total Profit
Total Orders
Total Sessions
Conversion Rate
Revenue per Session
Total COGS
Profit Margin
Total Refunds
Average Order Value
Total Pageviews
Pages per Session

And these additional measures for the website analysis:

New Sessions
Repeat Sessions
Repeat Session Rate
Important correction

For Total Revenue, we used:

SUM(orders[price_usd])

For Total Profit, don't use orders[price_usd] - order_items[cogs_usd] directly because they are at different grain levels. The safer calculation for the product/order-item analysis is:

Total Profit =
SUM(order_items[price_usd]) - SUM(order_items[cogs_usd])


